From b2ba8f2ebe49188ec71e24d01e274ec616c611c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MediaGuard <mediaguard@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:31:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MediaGuard: target .NET 8 (LTS)

Sonarr v4 targets .NET 6, which is out of support since November 2024. Retarget all
projects and build.sh to net8.0 (SDK 8.0.421, the same as the Radarr fork) with the
minimal changes the .NET 8 SDK requires:
- Microsoft.Extensions.*, ASP.NET Core and System.* package references to their 8.0
  versions (NLog.Extensions.Logging pulls Microsoft.Extensions.Logging 8.0 on net8.0)
- AuthenticationHandler constructors without the obsolete ISystemClock
- self-contained publish (on .NET 8 a runtime identifier no longer implies it; as in Radarr)
- queue filters null-safe: on .NET 8 an absent [FromQuery] array with default null stays
  null (GET /api/v3/queue without filters returned 500); same check as Radarr
- response headers set via the indexer instead of IDictionary.Add (ASP0019)
- SYSLIB0051 (formatter-serialization constructors) suppressed
- NuGet audit: the known SixLabors.ImageSharp 3.1.12 advisories are suppressed; it is the
  version Sonarr v4 already ships and 3.2.0 requires a commercial license key
